export const PRIVACY = "# Zome Privacy Policy\n\n**Last updated: 13 November 2026**\n\n**Who we are:** **Zome Lab Technology Ltd**, a company registered in Nigeria\n(RC 9907281), of Lagos, Nigeria (\"Zome\", \"we\"). We are the data\ncontroller for everything described here.\n**Contact, including any data protection enquiry:** privacy@myzome.app\n\n---\n\n## The short version\n\n- **Your data is stored securely in the European Union**, under the\n  protection of the Nigeria Data Protection Act.\n- **We never sell it, and we do not advertise.** There is no arrangement under\n  which anybody pays us for access to it, and no advertiser, insurer or employer\n  ever sees it.\n- **We keep what Care Purse and Care Fund need, and what the law asks of money\n  services.** Nothing more.\n- **You can delete your account from the app in two taps, and ask us for a\n  copy of everything at any time.** Deletion is immediate; protected backup\n  copies are gone within 35 days. Financial records the law\n  requires are kept, locked away, as §7 says.\n- **You must be 18.**\n\nThe rest of this document is the detail behind those lines.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Definitions\n\nThese words carry these meanings wherever they appear in this policy with a\ncapital letter.\n\n| Term | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| **Health Data** | Information about someone's physical or mental health. Under the NDPA this is *sensitive personal data*. In Zome it includes what an organiser writes about a patient's care on a Care Fund, and the record of which clinics, pharmacies and labs you paid. |\n| **Personal Data** | Any information relating to you as an identified or identifiable person. |\n| **Process** | Anything done with Personal Data, including collecting, storing, using, sharing and deleting it. |\n| **Processor** | A service provider that Processes Personal Data on our written instructions and for no purpose of its own. |\n| **we**, **us**, **our** | Zome Lab Technology Ltd (RC 9907281), of Lagos, Nigeria, the controller of your Personal Data. |\n| **you**, **your** | The person whose Personal Data this policy describes: someone with a Zome account, or someone who gives to a Care Fund or through a family link. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. In one paragraph\n\nZome helps people pay for care: Care Purse keeps money for your health and pays\nclinics, pharmacies and labs, and Care Fund lets family and friends help with a\nbig bill. Doing that means holding details about you and your money, and\nchecking who you are, as the law requires of money services. We hold what the\nproduct and the law need, we never sell it, no advertiser ever sees it, and\nyou can delete your account from the app in one action.\n\n**Zome does not read health data from your phone.** It does not connect to\nApple Health or Health Connect, and it does not track your activity, sleep or\nfood.\n\n**Zome is offered in Nigeria.** What protects your data is this policy and the\nNigeria Data Protection Act 2023.\n\n---\n\n## 3. What we hold\n\n### 3.1 What you give us, and what using Zome creates\n\n| What | Why we need it | Where it is |\n|---|---|---|\n| Email address | It is your account, and where your sign-in codes and receipts go | Kept by Zome |\n| Password *(optional)* | So you can sign in without waiting for an email | Kept by Zome, in a form we cannot read back — never as you typed it |\n| Your name and nickname | To greet you, and to show businesses and givers who you are | Kept by Zome |\n| Signing in with Apple or Google *(only if you choose to)*: the email address, and the name if they share it, that Apple or Google confirms to us | So you can sign in with that account | Kept by Zome |\n| The phones and browsers you have signed in on: the name each gives itself (such as \"Safari on iPhone\") and when it was last used | So we can ask for an email code the first time you sign in somewhere new, and tell you when someone signs in | Kept by Zome |\n| A notification token from your phone *(only if you allow notifications)* | To send you notifications | Kept by Zome |\n| Your phone number, checked by a code we send to it | So we know it's yours and can reach you about your account and your money | Kept by Zome |\n| Your BVN, and your NIN *(only if you give it)*: we check them against the official record, then keep them encrypted. We show you the record to confirm it is you; once you do, the name on it becomes your name on Zome, and we keep your age band (such as 25 to 34) and that you are 18 or over. We do not keep the record's photo, its phone number or its date of birth | To confirm you are who you say, as the law requires of money services, and that you are 18 or over | Kept by Zome |\n| A selfie *(only if you take one)*: sent to our identity partner to check it shows one live face and matches the photo on your BVN or NIN record. We do not keep the photo, only that it matched and how closely | To confirm you are who you say, and raise your Care Purse limits | Not kept |\n| Your next of kin *(only if you add one)*: their name, how they're related to you, and their phone number | So we can reach someone about your account and your money if we can't reach you | Kept by Zome |\n| Care Purse: each amount you add, your balance, and what came in and went out | So Care Purse can hold your money for care and show you exactly what happened to it | Kept by Zome |\n| A bank account you link to Care Purse *(only if you link one)*: the bank, the account number and the name on it | So money can be taken from it when you ask, never more than the limit you set | Kept by Zome |\n| Payments you make: who you paid (a business on Zome, or a bank account's name, bank and number), the amount, your note, and any bill or pay code involved | To make the payment, show you your receipts, and keep the records the law requires | Kept by Zome |\n| Your family link *(only if you make one)*, and the gifts that arrive through it | So family can send money to your Care Purse | Kept by Zome |\n| A Care Fund *(only if you start one)*: its title, story, goal and updates, who it is for (their first name only), and every gift and payment | To run the fund and show its page; see §3.2 | Kept by Zome |\n\n### 3.2 Family links and Care Fund: what others see, and what we keep about givers\n\n**What anyone can see on a Care Fund page:** its title, story, goal and\nupdates, the first name of the person it is for, the organiser's first name\nand the initial of their surname, what has been raised, each gift's amount\nwith the name the giver chose (or \"Anonymous\"), and every payment to a\nprovider. Never a giver's note, email or phone, and never a document. **On a\nfamily link page,** a giver sees only your first name and the initial of your\nsurname.\n\n**What we keep about a giver,** who needs no Zome account: the name they chose,\ntheir note, their email (for their receipt and to tell them where the money\nwent), and, for a gift of ₦500,000 or more, their full name and phone number,\nwhich the law asks of large gifts. When a gift arrives we also keep the bank\naccount it came from, as their bank passes it on, so that if Zome stops a fund\nwe can return each giver's share to them. Only Zome sees these; the organiser\nsees the name the giver chose, their note and the amount.\n\n**If you start a Care Fund for someone else,** you confirm they (or their\nguardian) agreed to their first name and their care being shown on the page.\nWrite only what is needed to explain the care; the page is public.\n\n### 3.3 Health information in what you do\n\nZome does not ask about your health. Two things can still reveal it, so we\ntreat them as Health Data:\n\n- **A Care Fund's story**, which describes a patient's care and is shown\n  publicly, with the patient's (or their guardian's) agreement.\n- **Your payment records**, which show which clinics, pharmacies and labs you\n  paid. They are seen only by you, the business you paid, and Zome.\n\n### 3.4 What we never collect\n\n- **Health data from your phone.** Zome does not connect to Apple Health or\n  Health Connect.\n- **Advertising identifiers.** There is no advertising in Zome and no ad network.\n- **Your location.** Zome never asks for it.\n- **Your contacts, microphone or photo library.** The camera is used only when\n  you choose to take the selfie for the identity check (§3.1: sent to our\n  identity partner, not kept).\n- **Third-party trackers.** There are none in the app.\n\n### 3.5 This website\n\nThe website at myzome.app sets no cookies and runs no analytics, advertising or\ntracking scripts. Its fonts are served from our own address, so visiting it tells\nnobody else that you did. Like any web server, ours sees your IP address, the page\nyou asked for and when, so it can send the page and keep the site safe; that is not\nlinked to any Zome account. Signing in, and everything in your account, happen in\nthe web app at app.myzome.app, under this policy. The web app keeps you signed\nin with one cookie that only it can read, and remembers your browser with a\nsecond, so it can ask for an email code when you sign in somewhere new; it uses\nno other cookies and no trackers.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Which law applies, and why we are allowed to hold it\n\nWe are a Nigerian company offering Zome in Nigeria, so the **Nigeria Data\nProtection Act 2023 (NDPA)** governs what we do, and the **Nigeria Data\nProtection Commission (NDPC)** is our supervisory authority.\n\nWe need a lawful basis for everything we hold, and for Health Data a further\ncondition on top of it.\n\n| What | Lawful basis | Condition for Health Data |\n|---|---|---|\n| Your account: email, password, name, sessions, devices you sign in on | Performance of our contract with you | Not Health Data |\n| Care Purse, payments, family links and Care Fund | Contract, and the legal obligation to keep financial records | Payment records: needed to provide the service you asked for, and to meet the law on financial records |\n| A Care Fund's story | Contract with the organiser | **Explicit consent** of the patient or their guardian, which the organiser confirms — NDPA s.30(1)(b) |\n| BVN, NIN, selfie and phone checks; large givers' details | Legal obligation (anti-money-laundering rules) | Not Health Data |\n| Sign-in notices and abuse prevention | Legitimate interests — keeping your account and money safe | Not Health Data |\n| Fault reporting | Legitimate interests — knowing when the product is broken | Not Health Data; see §6 |\n| Usage analytics | Legitimate interests — knowing which parts of Zome are used | Not Health Data; see §6. **You can turn it off in Settings → Privacy.** |\n\n### 4.1 Decisions made by rules\n\nHow much your Care Purse can hold and pay in a day follows fixed rules about\nwhich checks you have completed (§3.1). No person looks at each case, so we\nsay so. If you think a limit is wrong for you, write to privacy@myzome.app and\none of us will look.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Where it is, and when it leaves the country\n\n**Your data is stored in the European Union**, with service providers who\nprotect it under contract. A few providers that help us run Zome may handle\nlimited technical information elsewhere; they receive no more than they need,\nand the same safeguards apply.\n\nAs a Nigerian company we transfer your data out of Nigeria to hold it in the\nEU. We do so relying on the protection the EU regime provides and on the\ncontractual terms each provider gives us, as the NDPA permits.\n\n### 5.1 The safeguard we rely on\n\nEach provider that receives Personal Data outside Nigeria is bound by its\ncontract with us to protect it to a standard no lower than the NDPA requires,\nin addition to the terms described in §6. **You may ask for a copy of the\nterms that cover a particular transfer** by writing to privacy@myzome.app, and\nwe will provide them, with commercial terms removed.\n\nIf you need to know where a particular kind of data is held, ask us at\nprivacy@myzome.app.\n\n## 6. Who else sees it\n\n**People you deal with through Zome.** A business you pay sees your name, the\namount and any note. A provider paid by a Care Fund sees the fund's name and\nthe amount. Anyone can see a Care Fund's public page, as §3.2 describes.\n\n**The services that run Zome**, each acting as our processor under a contract\nthat binds them to our instructions. We describe them by what they do rather\nthan by name:\n\n| What they do | What they get | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| Hosting and secure storage | Everything, because the product runs on it, kept encrypted | Zome cannot run without it |\n| Email delivery | Your email address and what each email says: sign-in codes, receipts, notices about your account and money, and givers' receipts | To send you the email |\n| Identity checks | Your phone number, your BVN or NIN when you give them, your selfie if you take one, and your full name to match against the record | To send you a code and to check who you are |\n| Payment processing for Care Purse and Care Fund | Your full name, your email, and each amount you or a giver adds | To give an account to pay into, and to confirm what was paid |\n| Linking a bank account *(only if you link one)* | Your name, your email, and the bank account you link | To set up the direct debit you agree to with your bank |\n| Sending money to bank accounts | The account's bank, number and name, and the amount | To pay a bank account you choose, pay a provider from a Care Fund, pay a business, or return a giver's share |\n| Sign in with Apple or Google *(only if you use it)* | They confirm your email to us; we send them nothing about you | To sign you in |\n| Push notifications (Apple and Google) | Your phone's notification token and the words of each notification | To deliver notifications to your phone |\n| Fault reporting | Technical details of errors, with no personal data | To know when Zome is broken |\n| Usage analytics | Which screens are used and how far people get, with no identifier attached | To know which parts of Zome are worth building on |\n\n**Usage analytics is not about you.** It is a fixed list of things that can\nhappen in the app — a screen opened, a step finished — written into the app's\nsource in one file. It carries no name, no email and no amounts, and is not\nlinked to your account: events are counted and never gathered into a person.\n**You can turn it off at any time in Settings → Privacy**, and turning it off\nstops it on your phone immediately.\n\n**We do not sell your data. We do not share it with advertisers, insurers,\nemployers or data brokers. There is no arrangement under which anybody pays us\nfor access to it.** We share information with the authorities only where the\nlaw requires it, such as reports that anti-money-laundering rules oblige us to\nmake.\n\nIf you need the identity of a specific processor, ask us at privacy@myzome.app\nand we will tell you.\n\n---\n\n## 7. How long we keep it\n\n| What | How long |\n|---|---|\n| Your account and everything in it | Until you delete it |\n| Sign-in codes | 10 minutes, then deleted; single use |\n| Sessions | On a phone, 30 days or until you sign out; on the web, 15 minutes with nothing done and 12 hours at most |\n| Remembered phones and browsers | Until you delete your account |\n| Protected backup copies | Up to 35 days, then deleted automatically |\n| Fault reports | 90 days |\n| Record that an account was deleted | Kept, with nothing in it that identifies you |\n| Care Purse | Your account cannot be deleted while Care Purse holds money, while money you sent is still being added, or while a bank account is linked, so nothing of yours is lost. Once you have used Care Purse, deleting your account closes it instead: your sign-in, devices, profile and next of kin are deleted as for anyone else, and your Care Purse records are kept unchanged for as long as the law requires, at least five years after the account closes. Who they belong to (your name, email and sign-in) is kept encrypted with a key held away from our systems, and opened only for an audit or when the law requires it |\n| Gifts, Care Fund records and givers' details | As Care Purse records: kept as long as the law requires financial records to be |\n\n### Account deletion and backup retention\n\nWhen you delete your Zome account or ask us to delete personal data, we remove\nit from the live service at once: it is no longer visible or usable anywhere\nin Zome.\n\n- **Backups: up to 35 days.** To protect the service against data loss, and\n  to keep the financial records the law requires, we keep protected backup\n  copies. A copy of deleted data may remain in them for up to 35 days, then it\n  is deleted automatically.\n- **Backups are only for disasters.** They are kept apart from the live\n  service, opened only by authorised staff to recover the whole service, and\n  never used to restore a single account, so a deletion can't be undone.\n- **Financial records the law requires.** The minimum records that Nigeria's\n  anti-money-laundering laws and SCUML's rules require, such as amounts given\n  or paid, when, and bank transfer references, are kept separately for as long\n  as the law requires, as described for Care Purse above.\n\n---\n\n## 8. How it is protected\n\nYour data is encrypted in transit and encrypted at rest. Passwords, session\ntokens and your payment PIN are stored in a form we cannot read back, so\nnobody, including us, can recover them.\nYour BVN and NIN are encrypted. Repeated guessing is blocked, and an account locks after repeated wrong attempts.\n\nThe first time you sign in on a phone or browser we have not seen, we email you\na code before letting you in, and we tell you by email and notification\nwhenever someone signs in. On the web you are signed out after 15 minutes with\nnothing done. Every payment needs your PIN. If you lose a device you can end\nevery session at once from Profile on the web (Sign out everywhere), or ask us\nto, without waiting for anything to expire.\n\nWe keep the specifics of how this is implemented out of this document on\npurpose. Naming a particular algorithm here would turn a security decision into\na published commitment we would have to keep accurate as the product changes,\nand would tell an attacker more than it tells you.\n\n## 9. What you can make us do\n\nYou have the right to see what we hold about you, correct it, have it deleted,\nrestrict or object to how it is used, take it elsewhere, and withdraw consent.\n\n**Deletion is in the app.** In the iPhone or Android app: Settings → Account →\nDelete account. It removes your sign-in, sessions, devices, profile and next\nof kin all at once, and keeps only the financial records §7\ndescribes. It cannot be undone and there is no grace period. Copies of the\ndeleted data stay in our protected backups for up to 35 days and are then\ndeleted with them (see \"Account deletion and backup retention\" in §7).\n\nWhat survives besides those records is a single line recording that *an*\naccount was deleted at a particular time, with nothing in it that connects to\nyou. That is what lets us evidence the deletion without keeping you.\n\n**A copy of everything.** Write to **privacy@myzome.app** and we send you\neverything we hold about you, in a file you can open and take elsewhere,\nwithin one month. Credentials such as your password and PIN are left out.\n\n**If you gave to a Care Fund or through a family link** without an account,\nwrite to privacy@myzome.app with the email you gave, and we will do the same\nfor what we hold about you.\n\nFor anything else, write to **privacy@myzome.app**. We answer within one month.\n\nYou can also complain to the **Nigeria Data Protection Commission**\n(ndpc.gov.ng).\n\n---\n\n## 10. Children\n\nZome is for adults. **You must be 18 or over to use it**, and we do not\nknowingly hold data about anyone younger. If we discover we have, we delete it.\n\nEighteen, deliberately. Nigeria's NDPA treats anyone under 18 as a child and\nrequires verifiable parental consent before processing their data, and money\nservices need an adult's BVN or NIN. We confirm your age from that record and\nkeep only that you are 18 or over and your age band — **not your date of\nbirth.**\n\nA Care Fund may be for a child's care. The organiser, as the child's parent or\nguardian or with their agreement, decides what is shown, and only the child's\nfirst name appears.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Changes\n\nIf we change this policy in a way that affects what we do with your data, we\nwill tell you in the app before it takes effect, and you will be asked to agree\nagain where the law requires it.\n"
